      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The orofacial dysfunction syndrome is a disease which may lead to symptoms of headache because of inadequate occlusomandibular functions or autonomous muscular incoordination. However the symptoms can easily be confused with other manifestations of complaints in the head. The symptom \"headache\" makes interdisciplinary diagnosis obligatory, decisive importance being attributed to dentistry and oral surgery."},
